# Fact patterns — FLSA overtime (FP-061, FP-062)

> Using Overtime_flsa as O

## FP-061 — 46 hours at $30: six hours at time and a half

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestFp061:
  output computation content O.Overtime

scope TestFp061:
  definition computation equals
    output of O.Overtime with {
      -- hours_worked_in_week: 46.0
      -- regular_rate: $30
    }
  assertion computation.overtime_pay = $270
  assertion computation.total_pay = $1,470
```

```catala-test-cli
$ catala test-scope TestFp061
┌─[RESULT]─ TestFp061 ─
│ computation =
│   Overtime {
│     -- overtime_pay: $270.00
│     -- total_pay: $1,470.00
│   }
└─
```

## FP-062 — 38 hours: no overtime

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestFp062:
  output computation content O.Overtime

scope TestFp062:
  definition computation equals
    output of O.Overtime with {
      -- hours_worked_in_week: 38.0
      -- regular_rate: $30
    }
  assertion computation.overtime_pay = $0
  assertion computation.total_pay = $1,140
```

```catala-test-cli
$ catala test-scope TestFp062
┌─[RESULT]─ TestFp062 ─
│ computation = Overtime {
│                 -- overtime_pay: $0.00
│                 -- total_pay: $1,140.00
│               }
└─
```
